# The website has a private-repo home (SimonRoseDorix/LiveolatorWebsite), but its 42 files are
# still TRACKED here and publish-website-release.ps1 edits changelog.json / site.ts in-tree, so
# every release commits its own website changes. Ignoring the directory therefore only broke
# `git add website/` while changing nothing about what is tracked — ignore rules do not untrack.
# Re-add these rules in the same commit that actually untracks the files and moves the release
# sync to a cross-repo flow. website/.gitignore already covers dist/, .astro/ and node_modules/.
